  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, where <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If&nbsp;<math><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;is onto, then the values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>&nbsp;lie in (given,&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi></math> is the natural domain of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
