  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Where,&nbsp;<math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br />i.e., <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />According to the given condition, <math><mi>y</mi></math> takes all real values, for real <math><mi>x</mi></math> .</p><p>In other words, the above quadratic equation in <math><mi>x</mi></math> should have real roots for every real <math><mi>y</mi></math><br />i.e., <math><mi>D</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math><br />i.e., <math><mn>36</mn><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math><br />i.e., <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>46</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math><br />i.e., <math><mi>D</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and coefficient of <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />i.e., <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>46</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />i.e., <math><msup><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>46</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow></math><br />i.e., <math><msup><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow></math><br />i.e., <math><mn>2</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>14</mn></math> and <math><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow></math><br />i.e., <math><mn>2</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>14</mn></math><br />Hence, <math><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is onto for <math><mn>2</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>14</mn></math></p>",
